From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui: CoreDispatcher, Colors, AccessibilitySettings

What Windows Terminal and the WinUI 2 controls it is built with ask of Windows.UI, in a XAML island. The thread's CoreWindow now has a CoreDispatcher: RunAsync and RunIdleAsync, from any thread, run their callback on the CoreWindow's thread from its message loop, and their IAsyncAction completes when it has run (HasThreadAccess, ProcessEvents, the priority members and AcceleratorKeyActivated are there too). Windows.UI.Colors gives the named colours (the CSS colour keywords; Transparent is white with no alpha) and ColorHelper makes colours and names them. AccessibilitySettings says whether high contrast is on, and has the weak references C++/WinRT's event revokers take of it.
---
diff --git a/dlls/windows.ui/Makefile.in b/dlls/windows.ui/Makefile.in
index c4b5b38..2b0e1bc 100644
--- a/dlls/windows.ui/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/windows.ui/Makefile.in
@@ -3,8 +3,12 @@ IMPORTS = combase advapi32 user32 gdi32 oleaut32 uuid
 DELAYIMPORTS = shell32 shlwapi version windowscodecs
 
 SOURCES = \
+	accessibility.c \
 	classes.idl \
+	colors.c \
+	colors_classes.idl \
 	corewindow.c \
+	dispatcher.c \
 	thread_corewindow.c \
 	toast_classes.idl \
 	xmldom_classes.idl \
